Aerie-Purpose: Add the Crash reports section to Settings: a top-level route, its menu entry, its place in the page switcher, its strings, and the message handler that lists, deletes and opens the folder of the crash reports on this device.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (route.ts, router.ts, lazy_load.ts, BUILD.gn, settings_menu/settings_menu.html, settings_main/settings_main.html), chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_ui.cc, settings_localized_strings_provider.cc, BUILD.gn), chrome/app (generated_resources.grd and its gritdeps)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #262. The page, settings-aerie-crash-reports-page, is a Lit element in the overlay
(chrome/browser/resources/settings/aerie_crash_reports_page), wired the way the Aerie Guard page is
(adblock/0023): a section of the basic page at /crashReports, a menu entry after Aerie Guard, the
page switcher slot. The message handler, AerieCrashReportsHandler (overlay,
chrome/browser/ui/webui/aerie_crash_reports), is a plain message handler on chrome://settings only
that reads the Crashpad database of this device through components/aerie_crash_reports. It lists
the time, process type and version of each report, deletes one or all, and opens the folder. It
returns no contents of a dump and no path, and nothing it does touches the network. The strings
are in the overlay's aerie_crash_reports_strings.grdp, which this patch includes in
generated_resources.grd and hands to the page. docs/crash-reports.md has the whole account.

